# Atuin moved from the setup.atuin.sh curl installer to mise. That installer
# put a copy in ~/.atuin/bin and we shipped a conf.d stub to source its PATH
# entry, so both are now stale. Unmanaging a file does not delete it, so
# without this the orphaned binary and PATH stub linger on every machine that
# applied them, and the ~/.atuin/bin copy would shadow the mise-managed one.
# Only bin is purged: atuin itself writes ~/.atuin/logs (its default since
# 18.13), so removing all of ~/.atuin would flap on every apply.
.config/fish/conf.d/atuin.env.fish
.atuin/bin
.atuin/bin/**

